# Generated previews and one-off build logs
office_preview.png
basement_preview.png
room.log
snap.log

# Automatic copies taken before any scene regeneration
SceneBackups~/

# Installers and binaries never belong in the project tree. A 1.8 GB Rider installer
# was once downloaded into Art/Background and swept into a commit, which made the push
# impossible rather than merely slow: GitHub rejects any single file over 100 MB.
*.exe
*.msi
*.dmg
*.pkg

# Imported Asset Store packs stay local. The repo is public and their EULAs generally
# forbid redistributing the source assets, so the repo carries the game and the art
# that belongs to it, not somebody else's kit. A fresh clone will therefore show the
# office furniture as missing references until the packs are imported again.
/Assets/Brick Project Studio/
/Assets/Brick Project Studio.meta
/Assets/JustPlay/
/Assets/JustPlay.meta
/Assets/LowPolyOfficeProps_LITE/
/Assets/LowPolyOfficeProps_LITE.meta
/Assets/TDG Storage Solutions/
/Assets/TDG Storage Solutions.meta
/Assets/WindowAndDoorsPack01/
/Assets/WindowAndDoorsPack01.meta
/Assets/nappin/
/Assets/nappin.meta
/Assets/Awb-Free Low Poly Vehicles/
/Assets/Awb-Free Low Poly Vehicles.meta
/Assets/Dudes/
/Assets/Dudes.meta
/Assets/CharCrafter – Free Preset Characters Pack (Vol. 1)/
/Assets/CharCrafter – Free Preset Characters Pack (Vol. 1).meta

# Test results are regenerated on every run, so tracking them means every test run
# dirties the tree and blocks a rebase.
TestResults.xml
PlayResults.xml
Probe.xml
Drift.xml

# Private notes. Working material for store pages and devlogs, not for the public repo.
# CLAUDE.md is already untracked for the same reason.
GAME_GEMS.md

# Rendered proof frames and ad-hoc test results. Local verification, never shipped.
HubProof~/
PortraitProof~/
edit.xml
play.xml
CityProof~/
ScreenProof~/
CityFlight~/
TabProof~/

# Measured reports and per-fixture result files. Written by test runs, regenerated on demand,
# and never a source of truth: the fixture that writes them is.
CampaignProbe~/
ProbeResults*.xml
Alone.xml
Base.xml
Store.xml
UiFlight~/
Videos~/

# Reference screenshots of other people's products. They carry somebody else's branding and
# sometimes the author's own account details, and this repository is public. Keep them on the
# desktop and out of the tree.
Assets/_ScalingLaws/Art/ai_browser.png
Assets/_ScalingLaws/Art/ai_browser.png.meta
StoreShots~/
StakeShot~/

# The player itself. Hundreds of megabytes rebuilt from the source beside it, and this
# repository is public.
Build~/
build.log

# The PlayMode runner writes a scratch scene into Assets/ and deletes it when the run
# ends. A run that is interrupted leaves it behind, and it is untracked and named like a
# real scene, so it is exactly the kind of file that gets swept into a commit by a `git
# add -A` on a tired evening.
Assets/InitTestScene*.unity
Assets/InitTestScene*.unity.meta
smoke.log
icon.log

# Unity writes a .meta beside any stray file that lands under Assets/. A batchmode run
# started from the wrong directory drops its log there, and the meta is not ignored by *.log.
*.log.meta
